1
00:06:43,199 --> 00:06:49,199
America was born in the streets.

2
00:13:26,399 --> 00:13:32,399
Gangs of New York is a drama, history, crime film directed by Martin Scorsese.

3
00:20:09,599 --> 00:20:15,599
In early 1860s New York, Irish immigrant Amsterdam Vallon is released from prison and returns to the Five Points,
seeking revenge against his father's killer, William Cutting, a powerful anti-immigrant gang leader.

4
00:26:52,799 --> 00:26:58,799
He knows that revenge can only be attained by
infiltrating Cutting's inner circle.

5
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:42,000
Vallon's journey becomes a fight for personal survival
and to find a place for the Irish people.

6
00:40:19,199 --> 00:40:25,199
Amsterdam Vallon, played by Leonardo DiCaprio.

7
00:47:02,400 --> 00:47:08,400
Bill 'The Butcher' Cutting, played by Daniel Day-Lewis.

8
00:53:45,599 --> 00:53:51,599
Jenny Everdeane, played by Cameron Diaz.

9
01:00:28,799 --> 01:00:34,799
Boss Tweed, played by Jim Broadbent.

10
01:07:12,000 --> 01:07:18,000
Happy Jack, played by John C. Reilly.

11
01:13:55,199 --> 01:14:01,199
Johnny Sirocco, played by Henry Thomas.

12
01:20:38,399 --> 01:20:44,399
Gangs of New York is a 2002 epic historical drama film directed by Martin Scorsese and written by Jay Cocks,
Steven Zaillian, and Kenneth Lonergan, based on Herbert Asbury's 1928 book The Gangs of New York.

13
01:27:21,599 --> 01:27:27,599
The film stars  Daniel Day-Lewis, Leonardo DiCaprio, and
Cameron Diaz, along with Jim Broadbent, John C.

14
01:34:04,800 --> 01:34:10,800
Reilly, Henry Thomas and Brendan Gleeson in supporting roles.

15
01:40:48,000 --> 01:40:54,000
The film also marks the start of a collaboration between DiCaprio and Scorsese.

16
01:47:31,199 --> 01:47:37,199
The film is set from 1862 to 1863, when a long-running Catholic–Protestant feud erupts into violence, just
as an Irish immigrant group is protesting the threat of conscription during the Civil War.

17
01:54:14,399 --> 01:54:20,399
Scorsese spent 20 years developing the project until
Miramax Films acquired it in 1999.

18
02:00:57,599 --> 02:01:03,599
Principal photography took place in Cinecittà Studios in
Rome, and Long Island City, New York City.

19
02:07:40,800 --> 02:07:46,800
Gangs of New York was completed by 2001 but its release was
delayed due to the September 11 attacks.

20
02:14:24,000 --> 02:14:30,000
The film was theatrically released in the United States on
December 20, 2002, and grossed $193.8 million worldwide.

21
02:21:07,199 --> 02:21:13,199
It was met with generally positive reviews, and
Day-Lewis's performance was highly acclaimed.

22
02:27:50,399 --> 02:27:56,399
It received 10 nominations at the 75th Academy Awards, including Best Picture, Best Director
for Scorsese and Best Actor for Day-Lewis, but did not win in any category.

23
02:34:33,600 --> 02:34:39,600
The film explores themes of rescue, immigrant, ship, fire, army.

24
02:41:16,799 --> 02:41:22,799
The tone is emotional.
